{
    "file": "Measuring_ROI_of_Training.docx",
    "title": "Measuring ROI of Training",
    "duration": "3 Days",
    "overview": [
        "Training investments are increasingly expected to demonstrate measurable contribution to individual and organizational performance. Attendance, participant satisfaction, and completion rates provide useful information, but they do not by themselves show whether learning was applied, performance improved, business results changed, or the financial value of the intervention justified its cost.",
        "This three-day course provides a practical framework for evaluating training effectiveness and measuring return on investment. Participants examine the complete evaluation chain from needs and objectives through reaction, learning, application, business impact, cost analysis, benefit conversion, ROI calculation, and reporting. Particular attention is given to isolating the effects of training so that impact claims remain credible.",
        "Through practical exercises, evaluation planning, data analysis, benefit calculations, ROI cases, and reporting activities, participants learn how to build an evaluation approach that is proportionate to the importance and cost of the training intervention and useful to management decision makers."
    ],
    "audience": [
        "Training and development managers, learning and development professionals, HR managers and specialists, talent-development professionals, training coordinators, organizational-development professionals, performance-management specialists, internal trainers, HR business partners, and managers responsible for evaluating the effectiveness and business contribution of training programs."
    ],
    "methodology": [
        "The course uses an applied methodology combining short presentations, evaluation case studies, objective-setting exercises, evaluation-plan development, data-collection design, learning and performance measurement exercises, impact-isolation techniques, cost and benefit calculations, ROI calculations, reporting practice, group discussion, and action planning. Participants progressively build an evaluation and ROI framework for a realistic training intervention."
    ],
    "competencies": [
        "Training evaluation",
        "Learning measurement",
        "Performance-impact assessment",
        "Evaluation planning",
        "Data collection and analysis",
        "Impact isolation",
        "Training cost analysis",
        "Benefit conversion",
        "ROI calculation",
        "Evaluation reporting",
        "Stakeholder communication",
        "Evidence-based L&D decision making"
    ],
    "objectivesIntro": [
        "By the end of the course, participants will be able to:"
    ],
    "objectives": [
        "Explain the purpose and levels of training evaluation.",
        "Link training needs, learning objectives, performance outcomes, and business measures.",
        "Select appropriate evaluation measures for different training interventions.",
        "Measure participant reaction and learning without confusing them with business impact.",
        "Assess whether learning is transferred and applied in the workplace.",
        "Identify business-impact measures connected with training objectives.",
        "Use practical methods to isolate the effects of training from other influences.",
        "Identify and calculate the full costs of a training intervention.",
        "Convert appropriate training benefits into monetary values.",
        "Calculate benefit-cost ratio and return on investment.",
        "Report tangible and intangible results credibly to stakeholders.",
        "Develop a practical evaluation and ROI plan for a training program."
    ],
